A||||2||montage||Choice of Wheels||||1||
Z||000000||montage||03-08-2001||09:43 AM||||I have been planning on a wheel/tire upgrade for my 1988 formula and have decided on 225/40/16 for the front, 245/35/17 for the rear. I am having trouble deciding on the proper wheel that will fit. Most web sites that offer wheels will only let you search based on car make and stock tires. I was thinking on 16X7 front and 17X8 rear but need to know what offset works and what offset one could find. I calculated the front would need a 58 mm offset and the rear would need a 48 mm offset to keep the tire edge even with the outside of the fender. Could I please get some recommendations from the members on offset taht work and places to find the wheels in question. I know some members have these size tire widths but do not list the wheel size and offset they use, this would be very useful to me. Thanks! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||03-08-2001||10:38 AM||||Stock Formula offsets are 37MM front and 41MM rear.<BR>I have 17x7 with 40MM offset front & rear in my Formula & looks great. I'm not sure that your calculated offsets may work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||03-08-2001||11:21 AM||||i have 16x7.5 on two fieros. one set i got new and they have a 35mm offset, which i've noticed dosen't match what other people say but thats what the box said. the other set i got used. they were on a vw but i don't know the offset. they fit good though.  <P><BR>i also have 225/40-16's on the front of one car and 225/50-16's on the other. the 40 series is too small to me. i guess you can lower it all you want but to me they still look way too small for the wheel well opening. the 50 series fit well but might be a problem if i lower it, but i may have to consider that i probaly have the original front springs and they may be sagging some (something like 120,000 mls), leading me to think that a further drop would make the car lower than it actually would end up being with new lowered springs.<P>i hope to split the difference and find 225/45-16's. a few companies make them.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)||||reg||1
